# Architecture Principles

Follow these principles in every implementation.

* Clean Architecture
* Domain Driven Design (DDD)
* SOLID Principles
* Repository Pattern
* Service Layer Pattern
* Dependency Injection
* API First Design
* Versioned APIs
* Async First
* Secure by Default

Never violate these principles.

---

# Backend Folder Structure

Always follow this architecture.

app/

api/

core/

config/

database/

models/

schemas/

repositories/

services/

ai/

integrations/

storage/

middleware/

exceptions/

utils/

background/

tests/

Never place business logic inside API routes.

Never place SQL queries inside services.

Repositories communicate with the database.

Services implement business rules.

Routes only orchestrate requests and responses.

---

# Coding Standards

Always write production-quality code.

Every class must have a single responsibility.

Every function should be small and focused.

Use proper naming conventions.

Always include:

* type hints
* docstrings
* structured logging
* meaningful comments where required
* error handling

Avoid duplicated logic.

Prefer reusable services.

Prefer composition over inheritance.

---

# Database Rules

Use PostgreSQL.

Use SQLAlchemy Async ORM.

Use UUID primary keys.

Every table must include:

* id
* created_at
* updated_at
* created_by
* updated_by
* deleted_at
* version

Support:

* soft delete
* audit history
* versioning
* optimistic future scalability

Use JSONB only for dynamic AI-generated data.

Do not store relational data in JSON.

---

# API Rules

Design RESTful APIs.

Use versioning.

Example

/api/v1/

Every endpoint must include:

* authentication
* authorization
* validation
* structured responses
* proper HTTP status codes
* consistent error handling

Always generate OpenAPI-compatible APIs.

---

